  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour regulator reporting and 72-hour customer notice for all incidents. S2 sets a 55°C test and a 5% review trigger, but above-limit models are not automatically banned and per-model results go to regulators and purchasers, not the public. S3 allows six years for retrofits, S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months, and S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents per 100,000 with 72-hour notices."
